    {
      "bbox": [
        266,
        801,
        1495,
        1011
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Whereas, Employees of the New York City Transit Authority and the Manhattan and Bronx Surface Transit Operating Authority have threatened to commence an unlawful strike on December 15, 1999, and such strike would effectively cease all subway and bus services provided by the New York City Transit Authority and the Manhattan and Bronx Surface Transit Operating Authority; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 20,
          "mean": -0.2868,
          "min": -1.5136
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 69,
          "mean": -0.0052,
          "min": -0.3519
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 16999,
        "area_px": 257040,
        "density": 0.06613,
        "chars": 375,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 22.06
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        266,
        1026,
        1493,
        1125
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Whereas, It is necessary to insure public safety and the orderly transportation of people and goods in the City of New York; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.246,
          "min": -1.4911
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0001
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 26,
          "mean": -0.0009,
          "min": -0.0126
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 4639,
        "area_px": 121077,
        "density": 0.03831,
        "chars": 128,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 27.59
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        266,
        1139,
        1497,
        1503
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Whereas, The threatened strike would cause an increase in the response time of emergency vehicles which will endanger the lives and health of the City's residents, commuters and visitors, the loss of instructional time for more than one million students, wide-scale inability to gain access to routine medical care, massive disruptions in the criminal and civil court systems, the loss of wages for hundreds of thousands of persons, the loss, on a daily basis, of hundreds of millions of dollars for businesses in the City, and millions of dollars per day of lost revenues for the City and the Board of Education, and millions of dollars per day in increased expenditures by the City of New York;",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2533,
          "min": -1.4498
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 132,
          "mean": -0.0005,
          "min": -0.0493
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 21651,
        "area_px": 445038,
        "density": 0.04865,
        "chars": 696,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 32.15
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        268,
        1518,
        1493,
        1656
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Whereas, These circumstances constitute an imminent peril to the public health and safety requiring the adoption of special rules, regulations, procedures and restrictions as emergency measures; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2326,
          "min": -1.363
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0001
        },
        "text": {
